{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Some</b> say that the sense of \"eleven days from Horeb by the way of Mount Seir\" is that they journeyed in the wilderness forty years, and this is the meaning of \"And it was in the fortieth year.\" These have erred, for by Qadesh Barnea they arrived in the second year. Only, \"And it was in the fortieth year\" is joined to \"Moses spoke,\" and it seems to me that the correct interpretation is: \"These are the words\"—that is, the words of the commandments written in the sections \"See,\" \"Judges,\" \"When you go out,\" and \"When you come in\"—which he had already spoken when they were in the wilderness. And the phrase \"Moses spoke\" draws itself and what follows along with it. So too: \"These are the words that Moses spoke in the wilderness, in the Arabah, opposite Suf\"—from the day they departed from Sinai onward." "<b>Between Paran and between Tophel and Laban and Hatzerot and Di Zahav.</b> Places not mentioned in the portion of These Are the Journeys [Masei], or mentioned under other names. For behold, Senir [has] three names, and many [are] likewise."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Deleted duplicate; keeping only one translation per index."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:53.474066202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}